What is a custom exception?
A user-defined exception created by extending Exception (or another exception class) to represent application-specific errors.

Why create custom exceptions?
	• Better readability
	• Better debugging
	• Better business logic
	• Easier maintenance

Why should Exception be the last catch block?
Because it is the parent class. If placed first, the more specific catch blocks become unreachable.


