GARBAGE COLLECTION:
Garbage Collection (GC) is the process by which the JVM automatically removes objects from the Heap that are no longer being used.
	
Student s1 = new Student();
Student s2 = s1;
s1 = null;
s2 = null;

STACK -s1 = null, s2 = null
HEAP - Student Object
Now no references point to the object.
✅ It becomes eligible for Garbage Collection.

How Does the JVM Know?
The JVM starts from special references called GC Roots (such as local variables on the stack).
If an object can be reached from these roots, it is considered alive.
If it cannot be reached, it is considered eligible for collection.
For now, just remember:
	Reachable = Alive
	Not Reachable = Eligible for GC


